Verse 1:
[Eb]Teach, me, [Bb7/D]Father, what [Eb]to [Bb]say;
[Bb7]Teach me, Father, [Cm]how [Ab]to [Eb]pray;
[Eb]Teach [Fm]meall [Gm]along [Eb]the way
[Eb/Bb]How to be [Bb7]like Jesus.

Refrain:
[Eb]I [Gm/D]would [Cm]be [Gm/Bb]like [Ab]Jesus,
[Fm]I [Ab/Eb]would [Ddim]be [Ab/C]like [Bb]Jesus!
[Eb]Help [Gm/D]me, [Eb7/Db]Lord, to [Ab]daily [Fm]grow
[Eb/Bb]More and more like [Bb7]Jesus!

Verse 2:
[Eb]Teach me [Bb7/D]as [Eb]the [Bb7/F]days [Eb]go [Bb]by,
[Bb7]Teach me not to [Cm]reason [Eb]why,
[Eb]Teach [Fm]me [Gm]that [Ab]to [Eb]do and [Ab]die,
[Eb/Bb]Is to be [Bb7]like Jesus.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Teach me [Bb7/D]that [Eb]the [Bb7/F]time [Eb]is [Bb]short,
[Bb7]Teach me how to [Cm]live [Ab]and [Eb]work,
[Eb]Teach [Fm]me [Gm]that [Ab]to [Eb]never [Ab]shirk
[Eb/Bb]Is to be [Bb7]like Jesus.

Verse 4:
[Eb]Teach me [Bb7/D]how [Eb]we [Bb7/F]may [Eb]be [Bb]one,
[Bb7]Like the Father [Cm]and [Ab]the [Eb]Son;
[Eb]And [Fm]when [Gm]all [Ab]is [Eb]overcome,
[Eb/Bb]I will be [Bb7]like Jesus.
